            <pentabarf:title>Designing Custom Dashboard and Job Monitoring Tools in OOD</pentabarf:title>
            <pentabarf:subtitle></pentabarf:subtitle>
            <pentabarf:language>en</pentabarf:language>
            <pentabarf:language-code>en</pentabarf:language-code>
            <dtstart>20260310T113000</dtstart>
            <dtend>20260310T115500</dtend>
            <duration>002500</duration>
            <summary>Designing Custom Dashboard and Job Monitoring Tools in OOD</summary>
            <description>The default Open OnDemand dashboard has limitations in its customizability, and existing documentation focuses primarily on changes that can be made to the default OOD infrastructure. However, achieving true interface customization requires the use of HTML, Bootstrap JS, and CSS to enable complete control over design and functionality. Integrating these technologies with custom Slurm commands allows detailed statistics and other information about your HPC system to be displayed. This talk will cover the design, structure, and implementation details behind several custom pages: Dashboard: Custom pinned apps, an email-style Message of the Day system, and a system status widget. Jobs Monitor Page: Resources used by user jobs, total jobs queued/running/cancelled, and a searchable, sortable job list. System Status Page: Partition details and usage, available vs. used resources, and more.</description>
            <class>PUBLIC</class>
            <status>CONFIRMED</status>
            <category>Talk</category>
            <url>https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/YP3DSW/</url>
            <location>Breakout Room</location>
            
            <attendee>William Goldman [Tufts]</attendee>
            
        </vevent>
        
